      # What it is

      One of the three quantities a fusion adds up: stated as a claim, filed as the result of a
      calculation the receiver works out, or absent for a typed reason. `Demand/amount`,
      `Nameplate/amount` and `Jagged/draw` use it.

      # What it contains

      - `claim`: the figure, stated.
      - `derivation`: the figure is the result of a named calculation (`ComposedDerivation`).
        Sending a value as well would skip the calculation and could disagree with its inputs.
      - `absent`: why there is no figure (`ClaimAbsence`).

      # See also

      `StatedClaim` for the same choice where nothing computes the figure. `Identity` for what
      computes this one.
